{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetCfLtWnBiyL7TvH8beD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize the analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-27` — repository with save, findById, findAll methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — controller has create, getById, list; no confirm endpoint\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-84` — existing tests using MockMvc; tests both status and error.code\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum has ORDER/SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — converts ApiException to ApiError envelope with status code\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Error handling: Throws ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409); GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope\n2. Controller pattern: Direct repository usage (no service layer); POST create returns ResponseEntity with HttpStatus.CREATED; GET returns resource directly\n3. Testing: MockMvc for HTTP testing; assertions on both status code AND response body; failure tests assert error.code, not just status\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — add ErrorCode for shipment state violations (SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM or similar)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — add @PostMapping confirm endpoint \n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add 4 test cases covering the four scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n1. State machine must allow CREATED→CONFIRMED but reject CANCELLED\n2. Idempotency on already-CONFIRMED must succeed, not fail\n3. Error code must be appropriate for the domain (state conflict)\n\n**Open questions:** None — requirements clearly specify all four cases and their HTTP status codes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum to represent a state conflict when attempting to confirm a cancelled shipment. This makes the error machine-readable for clients and follows the pattern of existing codes.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method `confirmShipment(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. The method will:\n   - Fetch the shipment or throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - Check if status is CANCELLED and throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - Change status to CONFIRMED only if it's CREATED; if already CONFIRMED, leave unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Save the shipment and return it\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED`: POST confirm, assert 200 + body has CONFIRMED status, then GET to verify persistence\n   - `retry confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment`: Create and confirm, then confirm again, assert 200 + body still CONFIRMED, then GET to verify unchanged\n   - `rejects confirm of a CANCELLED shipment with 409`: Manually set shipment to CANCELLED, POST confirm, assert 409 + error.code is SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, then GET to verify state unchanged\n   - `rejects confirm of non-existent shipment with 404`: POST confirm with fake id, assert 404 + error.code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have added a separate service layer for shipment operations. Rejected because the existing codebase has direct repository usage in controllers, and adding a service would diverge from the established pattern and violate the \"preserve existing architecture\" constraint.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Exception |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | Shipment with CONFIRMED status, HTTP 200 | None |\n| Already CONFIRMED | repository.findById(id) | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) (no-op) | Shipment with CONFIRMED status, HTTP 200 | None |\n| CANCELLED state | repository.findById(id) checks status | Nothing (rejected before save) | ApiError with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code, HTTP 409 | ConflictException |\n| Not found | repository.findById(id) returns null | Nothing | ApiError with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code, HTTP 404 | ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Happy path confirms CREATED→CONFIRMED with persistence check (GET after POST)\n- Test 2: Idempotency on CONFIRMED succeeds and is stable (POST twice, verify no change on second GET)\n- Test 3: Rejected state (CANCELLED) returns 409 with correct error code and state remains unchanged (GET after rejected POST)\n- Test 4: Not found case returns 404 with correct error code\n\nEach test follows the skill requirement: exercise the call, re-read through a separate GET (except test 4 which reads a non-existent resource), and for rejections, assert the error code.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nI'll now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":22533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1200},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d27270e6-2a71-4ed2-a4fd-b8dfd5a3794d","uuid":"545d50ed-58ab-4943-b1d9-80001ec84f33","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:44:30.903Z","request_id":"req_011CetCfLBbmQLTWYrqpPqmy"}
