e)\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` — Added confirm endpoint (core of the feature)\n   - `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 4 test cases (required for testing)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum. **Had to change:** Yes, the feature requires a unique error code to distinguish this state violation from other 409 responses, making it part of the API contract.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` method with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. **Had to change:** Yes, this is the core requirement. The method:\n   - Correctly returns 404 via ResourceNotFoundException if shipment not found\n   - Returns 409 via ConflictException if CANCELLED, with appropriate error code\n   - Transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED via shipment.copy() immutable update pattern\n   - Preserves idempotency by not changing already-CONFIRMED shipments\n   - Returns the shipment as the response body (matches POST pattern of other create-like endpoints)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 new test methods. **Had to change:** Yes, the ticket requires tests and these cover all acceptance criteria. Each test follows the testing-and-verification skill:\n   - Tests assert response **body**, not just status\n   - State-changing tests include a **separate GET** to verify persistence\n   - Rejection test includes a **separate GET** to verify state was **unchanged**\n   - Rejection tests assert `error.code`, not just status\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met and all existing tests continue to pass.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement:** Add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED, idempotently handles already-CONFIRMED, rejects CANCELLED with 409, rejects non-existent with 404.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — Added SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code to distinguish state conflicts specific to shipment confirmation\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — Added confirm() endpoint that handles all four cases: transition, idempotency, rejection of CANCELLED, and 404 for not found\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 4 test cases covering CREATED→CONFIRMED transition with persistence verification, idempotent retry on CONFIRMED, rejection of CANCELLED with unchanged state, and 404 for non-existent shipment\n\n**Tests:**\n- `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status` — Verifies status-changing endpoint transitions shipment and persists via separate GET\n- `retry confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds` — Verifies idempotency: repeated call succeeds with no change to state\n- `rejects confirm of a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error code` — Verifies conflict response with correct error code and unchanged state via separate GET\n- `rejects confirm of non-existent shipment with 404 and error code` — Verifies not-found response with correct error code\n\n**Verification:** Command `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ passed with BUILD SUCCESS, all 17 tests run (9 in ShipmentControllerTest including 4 new), 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.\n\n**Not done:** Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no unrelated changes, no new dependencies."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3428,"cache_read_input_tokens":28794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3428},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d27270e6-2a71-4ed2-a4fd-b8dfd5a3794d","uuid":"03581fe0-7b84-44d8-9cfa-6bf4f99c4229","timestamp":"2026-09-09T16:45:21.892Z","request_id":"req_011CetCjGCbKZPSAH